\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. On wings of living light,
\par At earliest dawn of day,
\par Came down the angels bright,
\par All rolled the stone away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Your voices raise with one accord,
\par To bless and praise your risen Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The keepers, watching near,
\par At that dread sight and sound
\par Fell down with sudden fear
\par Like dead men to the ground:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Your voices raise with one accord,
\par To bless and praise your risen Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Then rose from death's dark gloom,
\par Unseen by mortal eyes,
\par Triumphant o'er the tomb,
\par The lord of earth and sky!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Your voices raise with one accord,
\par To bless and praise your risen Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Ye children of the light,
\par Arise with Him, arise!
\par See how the Daystar bright
\par Is burning in the sky!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Your voices raise with one accord,
\par To bless and praise your risen Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Leave in the grave beneath
\par The old times pass away;
\par Buried with Him in death,
\par O live with Him to-day!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Your voices raise with one accord,
\par To bless and praise your risen Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. We sing Thee, Lord Divine,
\par With all our hearts and powers,
\par For we are very Thine,
\par And Thou art ever ours.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Your voices raise with one accord,
\par To bless and praise your risen Lord.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

